course: dictionary
lesson: 13734
title: Growing stronger: intensify
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To intensify means to become stronger, greater or more extreme. It is a verb, so it changes its ending: intensify, intensifies, intensified, intensifying. Use it when something grows in strength, like a storm or a feeling.
explain: «The wind began to blow, and by lunchtime the storm had intensified.» The storm did not stop or start; it got stronger. Clue: the wind and the rain are getting worse, so intensified must mean grew stronger.
explain: You can also intensify something on purpose, which means to make it stronger. «The coach asked the team to intensify their efforts.» The team is being asked to try harder. To check your meaning, swap in «get stronger» or «grow more extreme». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Intensify means to become stronger, greater or more extreme.
fact: To intensify something means to make it stronger or more extreme.
fact: «The storm intensified» means the storm grew stronger.
fact: «Intensify efforts» means to try harder.
fact: «The pain intensified» means the pain got worse.
exercise: «The storm intensified during the night.» What does intensified mean here? | Moved away to the sea | *Became stronger | Became quieter | Stopped completely
exercise: The coach said, «We must intensify our efforts.» What should the team do? | Change the rules of the game | Give up for the day | Sit down and rest | *Try even harder
exercise: Find the past form of intensify. | stormy | intensifies | *intensified | intensifying
test: «The pain intensified as the hours passed.» What does intensified mean here? | Went away | *Got worse | Stayed exactly the same | Turned into a song
test: In a story, tension intensifies before the climax. What does this tell you? | The story becomes calmer | The characters go to sleep | The story ends at once | *The excitement and worry grow stronger
exam: Mia reads, «The heat from the lamp began to intensify, so she moved her hand away.» Which word best matches intensify here? | Stopped | Cooled down | Faded | *Grew stronger
